<p>
  This is the original firmware that is pre-installed on the Home Assistant
  Connect ZWA-2. It allows you to use the device directly connected to Home
  Assistant with the included USB cable.
</p>
<p>Follow this tutorial to restore the original firmware on your ZWA-2.</p>

<h3>Requirements</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <a
      href="https://www.home-assistant.io"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Home Assistant</a
    >
  </li>
  <li>
    <a
      href="https://www.home-assistant.io/connect/zwa-2/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >Home Assistant Connect ZWA-2</a
    >
  </li>
  <li>
    <a
      href="https://amzn.to/4mLqa6S"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >USB-C to C cable</a
    >
  </li>
</ul>

<p>To get started, follow these steps:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Make a backup of your Z-Wave network in Home Assistant.</li>
  <ol type="a">
    <li>
      You can do this on the
      <a
        href="https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/config_zwave_js/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Z-Wave config panel in Home Assistant</a
      >. Config → Devices & services → Z-Wave → Settings icon.
    </li>
    <li>Download backup is at the bottom of the page.</li>
  </ol>
  <li>Install the ESP Serial Bridge firmware</li>
</ol>
